{
  "description": "The hash= readers of Sessions 44 and older. Such a Session matched hash= against the drawn feature, and its Web writers filled the specific color rules (config.rules: qual, val) and the request's color and label override tables with drawn hashes (release 0.13.0: rendered IDs); hash= names the source-record hash now (release D-39). selectorCases pin the one mapper (session_io.source_hash_selector_value, sourceHashSelectorValue): a value, written <hash> or ^<hash>$ and maybe with rendered-ID record and instance suffixes, names the drawn features (rows of drawnFeatures: source hash, drawn hash, source index, record position) with that hash, ignoring case, in the record and with the source index its suffixes give; when they share one source hash that is not the value's own hash, the result names it in the same form without the suffixes. cases pin the Session draft reader (session_io.migrate_session_hash_rules, migrateSessionHashRules) with the shapes first-parent main wrote: feature catalog schema 3 and 4 rows (svgId, recordKey, biologicalFeatureId), Session 31-44 feature metadata, or the sources read again. Read by tests/test_session_compat.py and tests/web/feature-edit-migration.test.mjs.",
